00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:20.180
And then when he was a man, he stripped at your fictional bachelorette party.

178
00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:20.600
Okay.

179
00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:21.200
Okay.

180
00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:28.020
And then finally, there was Kevin's fiancé's daughter, Abby, who was played by Haley Daniels,

181
00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.400
who is Greg Daniels' daughter.

182
00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:32.820
Yes, Haley is so, so sweet.

183
00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:33.120
Yeah.

184
00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:34.400
And she did a great job.

185
00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:35.160
So good.

186
00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:36.060
She's not an actor.

187
00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:36.620
Not an actor.

188
00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:37.860
She did such a great job.

189
00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:40.720
She had to be very deadpan, and I thought she was hilarious.

190
00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:46.040
Fast fact number two, a lot of people ask, what was it like to do an episode with all

191
00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:46.860
these kids around?

192
00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:49.940
Now, what did you remember about that, Ange?

193
00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:56.040
Well, I mean, Haley was in our little accounting nook quite a bit, and I just wanted to make

194
00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:56.800
sure she was good.

195
00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:57.300
Yeah.

196
00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:00.440
I think I just wanted to make sure she was like, do you need to go to the bathroom?

197
00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:01.360
Do you have snacks?

198
00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.460
I just sort of became that person.

199
00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:03.840
Yeah.

200
00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:09.560
But obviously, when kids are in an adult work environment, you do change your behavior,

201
00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:10.620
or you should.

202
00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:11.580
Sorry.

203
00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:13.420
I remember we got a little lecture about it.

204
00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:13.800
Yeah.

205
00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:14.140
Oh.

206
00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:15.380
We got a little talking, too.

207
00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:16.320
We got a little talking, too.

208
00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:17.820
Actually, you're-

209
00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:18.840
At the beginning of filming.

210
00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:19.980
Yeah, at the beginning of filming.

211
00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:22.040
Just like, hey, guys, there's going to be kids on set.

212
00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:23.660
Let's just mind our manners today.

213
00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:28.380
And actually, when Michael and you have that scene in the cold open where you're like,

214
00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:33.600
Michael, I talked to you about this, that actually reminded me of whenever we had people

215
00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:34.520
visiting the set.

216
00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:35.120
Yeah.

217
00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:35.800
Whenever-

218
00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:37.900
Sometimes families would visit the set.

219
00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:42.060
They would win some type of visit, and a whole family would come.

220
00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:48.040
And a lot of times, our AD, Kelly Cantley, would be like, hey, everyone, heads up, young

221
00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:48.940
children.

222
00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:51.680
Keep it G-rated.

223
00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:56.680
Not that we were like a body group, but you know, it's like a group of adults all day.

224
00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:01.540
I feel like when there weren't kids around, though, there was quite a bit of cursing.

225
00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:02.380
There were.

226
00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:03.460
Yes, that's true.

227
00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:05.080
You know, so there were adult words.

228
00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:06.620
There were adult words.

229
00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:08.840
But besides that, we weren't-

230
00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:09.180
Yeah.

231
00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:11.840
Super, like, weird or inappropriate or anything.

232
00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.000
No, but our scripts were half the time.

233
00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:14.240
That's true.

234
00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:18.280
Half the time, there were things that were said within the context of a script where I'm

235
00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:18.740
like, ooh.

236
00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:19.560
Yeah.

237
00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:20.780
Yeah, that's true.

238
00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:21.300
Okay.

239
00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:22.380
All right.

240
00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:25.360
Fast fact number three, this was sent in by a fan.

241
00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:27.220
I loved this.

242
00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:29.400
Thank you so much, Kelly Nudo.

243
00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:36.100
She tipped me off to the fact that Fundle Bundle, you know, the little TV program that Michael

244
00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:41.820
was on as a child in this episode, it was inspired by a real local children's

245
00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:45.700
program in Scranton called The Land of Hatchimalatchee.

246
00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:47.020
Oh, my Lord.

247
00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:48.400
I love that.

248
00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:49.240
Yes.

249
00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:53.020
It was a little program for kids that started in the 50s.

250
00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:55.300
It ran for almost 25 years.

251
00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:55.920
Local.

252
00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:57.660
Local Scranton.

253
00:08:57.880 --> 00:08:58.040
Oh.

254
00:08:58.200 --> 00:08:58.420
Yes.

255
00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:02.780
It featured songs and appearances by kids, just like our version.

256
00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:07.560
It was originally hosted by a woman named Nancy Berg, who was referred to as Miss Nancy.

257
00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:13.860
And then it was hosted by Miss Judy, who was played by Lois Burns.

258
00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:17.660
I don't know why they called her Miss Judy when her name was Lois, but they did.

259
00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:23.080
And of course, in our version, we had Miss Trudy, who was played by actress Sue Nelson.

260
00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:24.760
And Edward R.

261
00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:25.940
Meow.

262
00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:27.020
Yes.

263
00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:30.280
But this was really sweet.

264
00:09:30.860 --> 00:09:35.940
Lois, who played Miss Judy, was interviewed recently about her time on The Land of Hatchimalatchee.

265
00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:37.420
And she said-

266
00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:38.360
